How To Build CustomOS and the CustomOS bootloader (Windows)

1. Download all of the files required
2. Make a folder somewhere to store all of the CustomOS files
3. Place the Compile.cmd script in the root of that folder.
4. Make a folder called "files" in the root of that folder.
5. Place all of the files in the "files" folder of this repository (files like .c, .h, .s) into your "files" folder.

Note! Make sure mingw-w64 is installed to the system PATH.

6. Run the Compile.cmd script, ensure it completes without any errors.
7. Find a way to run the bootx64.efi file, probably by running it in a VM (real hardware has not been tested).
   I recommend installing QEMU and running the "Run QEMU.cmd" file also included, because it works perfectly.

It will (at least hopefully) boot into the CustomOS bootloader, from there you can select to Boot CustomOS and then you can use CustomOS!
